				<!--
				  Transitive security pin. Not exposed as a Boot property, so it is pinned here
				  rather than in <properties>. It arrives through a dependency whose version we
				  do not control; drop the pin once that upstream ships the fixed version itself.

				  beanutils CVE-2025-48734. commons-validator 1.9.0 declares commons-beanutils
				          1.9.4, which is the vulnerable version. Fix: 1.11.0.

				  The bcprov pin that used to sit here was REMOVED, by exactly the rule above.
				  It was added for CVE-2025-14813 (CRITICAL) when spring-cloud-commons 4.3.1
				  brought the vulnerable 1.80. Under spring-cloud 2025.0.3, spring-cloud-commons
				  4.3.3 brings 1.80.2 on its own, and Trivy lists 1.80.2 as a fixed version
				  (fixes are 1.80.2 / 1.81.1 / 1.84). Upstream now satisfies it, so carrying our
				  own version here only creates a second thing to maintain: Dependabot had
				  already walked the pin to 1.85 (PR #26) purely because it existed.

				  If a future bcprov CVE needs a version newer than whatever spring-cloud-commons
				  ships, re-add the pin here rather than bumping spring-cloud for it. The
				  pr-build Trivy scan is what tells you.
				-->
				<dependency>
					<groupId>commons-beanutils</groupId>
					<artifactId>commons-beanutils</artifactId>
					<version>1.11.0</version>
				</dependency>
			</dependencies>
		</dependencyManagement>
	
